### `info()`
*Name, version, nu version, nu plugins, and the registered library/module/function hierarchy with call schemas.*

#### arguments

Schema (partial):
```json
{
  "properties": {},
  "required": []
}
```

#### Example

MCP (partial):
```json
{
  "arguments": {}
}
```

Output (partial):
```json
{
  "result": {
    "structuredContent": {
      "name": "nushell_mcp",
      "version": "0.0.40",
      "nu_version": "0.113.1",
      "plugins": [
        { "name": "empower", "version": "0.0.2" },
        { "name": "polars" }
      ],
      "libraries": [
        {
          "name": "emptwo",
          "path": "/home/box/ai/emptwo/nu/emptwo",
          "modules": [
            {
              "name": "git",
              "submodules": [],
              "functions": [
                {
                  "name": "commit",
                  "args_schema": { "repo_dir": "string", "files": ["string"], "commit_msg_filename": "string" },
                  "result_schema": { "commit": "string", "status": "string" }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "layout",
              "submodules": [],
              "functions": [
                { "name": "memories", "args_schema": {}, "result_schema": { "memories": ["string"] } }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "functions": []
        }
      ]
    },
    "content": []
  }
}
```

The `libraries` hierarchy is the live, version-matched `call()`
surface: each library carries `path` (the editable source dir) +
`modules` + root-level `functions`; each module carries
`submodules` + `functions`; each function carries its
`args_schema` + `result_schema` as structured JSON (the `## Schemas`
grammar; a void-args function reads `{}`). A library HAS modules; a
module MAY HAVE submodules. This is ground truth - prefer it over any
static library index, which is only a snapshot.

## Bootstrap: run info() first

`info()` returns the full, version-matched toolset for the current
session - server + nu versions, loaded plugins, and the entire
registered-library hierarchy with call schemas. The libraries
change between sessions; reading them live is how a fresh bootstrap
(or a subagent) learns exactly which `call()` targets exist now,
rather than trusting a static index that drifts.

Run `mcp__nushell__info()` on every bootstrap so the session knows its full toolset.
